               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 19-year-old male patient, admitted on 03/11/2009 with a one-day history of progressive right lower quadrant pain, nausea, and low-grade fever, clinically consistent with acute appendicitis. On admission, physical examination revealed rebound tenderness at McBurney's point. Blood tests confirmed leukocytosis, and abdominal ultrasonography supported the diagnosis of acute appendicitis. The patient was resuscitated with intravenous fluids, administered analgesic and antibiotic therapy, and subsequently underwent laparoscopic appendectomy on the same day without intraoperative complications. The postoperative course was uneventful. Wound care was provided, and the patient was mobilised early. He was discharged home on 04/11/2009 in good general condition with instructions for follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact me should any questions arise.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
